    <div class="bg-emerald-950/20 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500 border-y border-r border-emerald-500/30 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-xl mb-10">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 font-mono mb-2">
        ⚡ Quick Answer: GitHub Actions Concurrency
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed">
        To prevent rapid git pushes from queueing redundant builds, add top-level <code>concurrency</code> to your workflow YAML using <code>group: &#36;&#123;&#123; github.workflow &#125;&#125;-&#36;&#123;&#123; github.ref &#125;&#125;</code> and <code>cancel-in-progress: true</code>. For pull requests, scope the group to <code>github.head_ref || github.run_id</code> so main branch production deployments are never accidentally cancelled mid-flight.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Fail-Safe Branch & PR Concurrency Pattern</h2>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/90 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto mb-8">
      <pre is:raw>
name: Continuous Integration &amp; Tests

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

# Cancel outdated PR builds, but never cancel sequential main deploys
concurrency:
  group: &#36;{"{{"} github.workflow {"}}"} - &#36;{"{{"} github.head_ref || github.run_id {"}}"}
  cancel-in-progress: &#36;{"{{"} github.event_name == 'pull_request' {"}}"}

jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Run Test Suite
        run: npm test
      </pre>
